Low-grade duralite.

737
00:32:03,367 --> 00:32:05,800
 Well, at least we saved them 
 the cost of a crew of geologists.

738
00:32:05,800 --> 00:32:07,167
( chuckles ) 
We saved them more than that.

739
00:32:07,167 --> 00:32:08,200
( forced chuckling )

740
00:32:08,200 --> 00:32:09,767
 We increased the total fish catch 
 in this country

741
00:32:09,767 --> 00:32:11,333
by thousands of tons.

742
00:32:11,333 --> 00:32:12,900
I heard about that. 
How'd it happen?

743
00:32:12,900 --> 00:32:14,933
His face makes no sense.

744
00:32:14,933 --> 00:32:16,400
One of our instruments 
got a strange signal

745
00:32:16,400 --> 00:32:19,100
 - about 500 feet below the surface. 
 - Bob Vila.

746
00:32:19,100 --> 00:32:21,200
Turned out to be 
a large school of fish.

747
00:32:21,200 --> 00:32:23,400
 We turned the information over 
 to one of the fishing companies,

748
00:32:23,400 --> 00:32:26,500
 and now they're talking about 
 installing radar on all of their ships.

749
00:32:26,500 --> 00:32:28,333
I've always maintained 
there's no limit

750
00:32:28,333 --> 00:32:29,667
to the possibilities of radar.

751
00:32:29,667 --> 00:32:31,100
Now, where's 
the damn donut cart?

752
00:32:31,100 --> 00:32:33,267
- Has Bill Travis reported in? 
- Yes, sir.

753
00:32:33,267 --> 00:32:34,967
He thinks he has a lead 
on the murder gun

754
00:32:34,967 --> 00:32:36,000
in the Allen case.

755
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:37,967
We'd have an open-and-shut case

756
00:32:37,967 --> 00:32:39,333
if he could dig up that gun.

757
00:32:40,633 --> 00:32:43,933
"Your attention, please. 
You will love radar.

758
00:32:43,933 --> 00:32:46,733
Give yourselves to it freely."

759
00:32:46,733 --> 00:32:49,433
( sobbing ) 
"Just get out. Get out."

760
00:32:52,233 --> 00:32:56,833
"Oh, here's a lovely spot. 
I'll get the picnic lunch."

761
00:32:56,833 --> 00:32:59,967
 "Oh, would you look at that? 
 Billie Joe McAllister's down there."

762
00:33:04,867 --> 00:33:06,533
Whoever invented 
this seeing-eye gadget

763
00:33:06,533 --> 00:33:08,267
sure had it in for me.

764
00:33:08,267 --> 00:33:10,333
We've been covering 
this highway for 50 miles.

765
00:33:10,333 --> 00:33:11,433
Not a sign of the gun.

766
00:33:11,433 --> 00:33:13,967
 Ah, quit griping. 
 If we don't find it here, we'll quit.

767
00:33:13,967 --> 00:33:16,333
- Now you're talking. 
- Come back tomorrow.

768
00:33:16,333 --> 00:33:18,900
Look, we've got to find it. 
See what's cooking.

769
00:33:18,900 --> 00:33:20,233
Oh, my aching feet.

770
00:33:20,233 --> 00:33:22,533
Have you tried radar 
on your feet?

771
00:33:23,933 --> 00:33:25,533
 "It's amazing we can work together

772
00:33:25,533 --> 00:33:27,667
after all that's happened, 
eh, Gary?"

773
00:33:32,933 --> 00:33:35,200
- Hey, look. 
- I have water-weight gain.

774
00:33:35,200 --> 00:33:36,733
This thing is picking up 
a metallic reaction.

775
00:33:36,733 --> 00:33:38,100
It could be the gun.

776
00:33:38,100 --> 00:33:40,900
 We know that Allen 
 made his getaway over this road.

777
00:33:40,900 --> 00:33:42,900
Perfect spot to hide a gun, 
if you ask me.

778
00:33:42,900 --> 00:33:44,033
Keep working that thing 
and let me know

779
00:33:44,033 --> 00:33:45,600
when you hit the exact spot.

780
00:33:45,600 --> 00:33:47,633
Work your evil magic, 
radar thingy.

781
00:33:47,633 --> 00:33:50,733
- Okay, say when. 
- "Stella."

782
00:33:50,733 --> 00:33:53,067
Move over. More, more.

783
00:33:53,067 --> 00:33:55,067
Whoa. There you are. 
That's it.

784
00:33:55,067 --> 00:33:58,500
 "Ted. Ted. 
 Ted, I'll take you to a restroom.

785
00:33:58,500 --> 00:34:01,300
I thought you were over that."

786
00:34:01,300 --> 00:34:03,400
"Hey, I found Judge Crater."

787
00:34:03,400 --> 00:34:06,467
 "Peace on Earth" was all it said.

788
00:34:08,633 --> 00:34:11,100
"Blech! Want some?"

789
00:34:15,667 --> 00:34:17,933
( fanfare plays )

790
00:34:20,667 --> 00:34:23,567
Hey, I want to read that... Oh.

791
00:34:23,567 --> 00:34:27,267
Hmm. Evidence that Christ 
Himself invented radar.

792
00:34:27,267 --> 00:34:30,233
What do you know? 
Alien murder case, huh?

793
00:34:30,233 --> 00:34:34,067
Okay, you can turn it now. 
Turn it!

794
00:34:34,067 --> 00:34:35,167
Headquarters is very pleased

795
00:34:35,167 --> 00:34:37,233
with the help we gave 
in the Allen case.

796
00:34:37,233 --> 00:34:39,433
That's nice of them. 
At least it shows

797
00:34:39,433 --> 00:34:41,433
that with the improvements 
we've made in the telemeter,

798
00:34:41,433 --> 00:34:43,100
 we can work hand in glove 
 with any branch of the government.

799
00:34:43,100 --> 00:34:45,233
And should be a blow 
to organized crime, too,

800
00:34:45,233 --> 00:34:47,033
once they realize we can 
keep a check on them.

801
00:34:47,033 --> 00:34:48,967
- I hope so. 
- Great. Super.

802
00:34:48,967 --> 00:34:51,133
But there's still legwork 
that can be eliminated.

803
00:34:51,133 --> 00:34:53,667
That's for me. 
I don't like legwork.

804
00:34:53,667 --> 00:34:54,800
What do you expect to do?

805
00:34:54,800 --> 00:34:57,233
Stay home in bed and have 
radar do all the work?

806
00:34:57,233 --> 00:34:58,700
That's not a bad idea.

807
00:34:58,700 --> 00:35:00,233
Look, what we need 
is more equipment.

808
00:35:00,233 --> 00:35:01,600
"Stuff. Things."

809
00:35:01,600 --> 00:35:04,167
A lot of what we do could be 
done better by radar.

810
00:35:04,167 --> 00:35:07,533
That's only a matter of time. 
After all, we're infants

811
00:35:07,533 --> 00:35:10,067
in this new field 
of scientific detection.

812
00:35:10,067 --> 00:35:12,067
We must crawl 
before we can walk.

813
00:35:12,067 --> 00:35:14,233
- "And now I need my binky." 
- Don't mention "walk."

814
00:35:14,233 --> 00:35:15,633
 You can't blame me for dreaming.

815
00:35:15,633 --> 00:35:17,267
No, not at all.

816
00:35:17,267 --> 00:35:18,300
And a lot of those dreams 
have come true

817
00:35:18,300 --> 00:35:19,767
in the last few years,

818
00:35:19,767 --> 00:35:21,967
 like the image we get on our screen.

819
00:35:21,967 --> 00:35:24,733
 And to think that Dick Tracy used it 
 before it was invented.

820
00:35:24,733 --> 00:35:27,100
And don't forget 
Flash Gordon and Buck Rogers.

821
00:35:27,100 --> 00:35:29,200
"And Lawrence Hilton-Jacobs 
and Roddy McDowall

822
00:35:29,200 --> 00:35:31,200
and Raoul Wallenberg and..."

823
00:35:31,200 --> 00:35:33,133
"Any Farm Kid, U.S.A."

824
00:35:36,033 --> 00:35:38,467
Oh, dinner at 
the Homesick Restaurant.

825
00:35:38,467 --> 00:35:41,233
Radar knows 
what you want to order.

826
00:35:41,233 --> 00:35:45,767
How'd she get into 
that waitress outfit so fast?

827
00:35:45,767 --> 00:35:47,700
Her head's a butter sculpture.

828
00:35:50,400 --> 00:35:52,633
♪ There's a new girl in town ♪

829
00:35:52,633 --> 00:35:54,700
♪ She's looking good! ♪

830
00:35:54,700 --> 00:35:56,300
Anything special today?

831
00:35:56,300 --> 00:35:58,300
- You! 
- The White House surprise.

832
00:35:59,600 --> 00:36:03,333
"Mm, what's your soup 
du jour of the day?"

833
00:36:03,333 --> 00:36:06,133
"We're out of Salisbury steak?"

834
00:36:06,133 --> 00:36:08,833
"Material: 10 yards 
of dotted Swiss. Hmm."

835
00:36:08,833 --> 00:36:12,300
Mm, sounds interesting. 
I'll order later.

836
00:36:12,300 --> 00:36:13,833
"Well, I'm gonna cash out.

837
00:36:13,833 --> 00:36:15,900
Blanche will be by 
to take care of you."

838
00:36:15,900 --> 00:36:18,500
 "I could read that a thousand times."

839
00:36:21,600 --> 00:36:25,533
 ♪ I get too hungry for dinner at 8:00 ♪

840
00:36:25,533 --> 00:36:27,767
( humming )

841
00:36:30,967 --> 00:36:33,167
Hey, it's the Boy Luck Club.

842
00:36:33,167 --> 00:36:36,067
( chuckles ) 
Well, I enjoyed it.

843
00:36:36,067 --> 00:36:39,033
( phone rings )

844
00:36:39,033 --> 00:36:41,500
"Send up some gas juice. 
You know, laugh water."

845
00:36:41,500 --> 00:36:43,733
- Hello. 
- "Yes, is Sid Melton there?"

846
00:36:43,733 --> 00:36:45,933
Yeah. Yeah, fine.

847
00:36:45,933 --> 00:36:47,800
I'll take it from here, honey.

848
00:36:47,800 --> 00:36:50,400
- See you later. 
- That was Honey West.

849
00:36:50,400 --> 00:36:53,267
Violet's cooked up 
another job for us.

850
00:36:53,267 --> 00:36:55,433
"Hey, quit flashing 
the neighbors back there."

851
00:36:55,433 --> 00:36:56,633
 We'll meet here in a couple hours.

852
00:36:56,633 --> 00:36:58,733
I'll have the layout 
worked out for us.

853
00:36:58,733 --> 00:37:01,333
"We need something to 
drab the room up."

854
00:37:01,333 --> 00:37:03,800
 I think I'll put on the feedbag.

855
00:37:03,800 --> 00:37:05,933
 I wish I was in love with a gal 
 that worked in a restaurant.

856
00:37:05,933 --> 00:37:08,667
- Free eats. 
- Yep. Aim high, Ted.

857
00:37:08,667 --> 00:37:09,933
( chuckles )

858
00:37:09,933 --> 00:37:12,067
♪♪

859
00:37:18,667 --> 00:37:22,500
- Oh, boy. 
- ( coughing )

860
00:37:22,500 --> 00:37:24,267
Hey, Pill Box, want to 
go to lunch with me?

861
00:37:24,267 --> 00:37:25,733
Oh, no, doctor's orders.

862
00:37:25,733 --> 00:37:28,800
I got to take my fresh-air 
deep-breathing exercises.

863
00:37:28,800 --> 00:37:30,533
I have to hurt you now.

864
00:37:30,533 --> 00:37:32,633
 - You know the window's closed. 
 - Huh?

865
00:37:32,633 --> 00:37:35,067
I said, the window is closed.

866
00:37:35,067 --> 00:37:37,067
- Oh, you got to open it? 
- ( imitates rim shot )

867
00:37:37,067 --> 00:37:40,433
"I'm gonna go have lunch 
with Morey Amsterdam."

868
00:37:40,433 --> 00:37:42,700
( clears throat ) 
Pardon me, is this booth taken?

869
00:37:42,700 --> 00:37:45,000
Blackie. 
Gee, I'm glad to see you.

870
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:46,533
"Did you bring that tip 
you owe me?"

871
00:37:46,533 --> 00:37:47,967
We're going on a job 
this afternoon.

872
00:37:47,967 --> 00:37:49,000
Yeah, I know.

873
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:51,033
What's the matter? 
Aren't you happy?

874
00:37:51,033 --> 00:37:52,500
If this pans out, 
we'll have enough dough

875
00:37:52,500 --> 00:37:53,800
to get married 
and blow this town.

876
00:37:53,800 --> 00:37:54,833
Do you mean that?

877
00:37:54,833 --> 00:37:56,400
 It's what I've been telling you 
 all the time.

878
00:37:56,400 --> 00:37:58,733
One more good job, 
and we can quit this racket.

879
00:37:58,733 --> 00:38:02,467
- Looks like this is it. 
- I'm so happy.

880
00:38:02,467 --> 00:38:06,167
"Employees must wash tongues 
before returning to work."

881
00:38:06,167 --> 00:38:07,533
Wow!

882
00:38:07,533 --> 00:38:10,233
- Okay. 
- All: We're next.

883
00:38:10,233 --> 00:38:12,967
- Uh, come in. 
- "I'll have the French dip."

884
00:38:12,967 --> 00:38:15,800
 "I'll have the tongue sandwich, 
 if there's any left."

885
00:38:15,800 --> 00:38:16,867
How'd you get this?

886
00:38:16,867 --> 00:38:19,300
I told you about the plant 
I had at the restaurant.

887
00:38:19,300 --> 00:38:20,967
A lot of important people 
eat there,

888
00:38:20,967 --> 00:38:22,767
 and eventually some of them talk.

889
00:38:22,767 --> 00:38:24,367
Cheetah. Mm.

890
00:38:24,367 --> 00:38:27,133
 I'm beginning to wonder 
 how I ever got along without you.

891
00:38:27,133 --> 00:38:29,000
And I was beginning to wonder

892
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:30,300
when you were going to 
realize it.

893
00:38:30,300 --> 00:38:34,267
No, no, no! 
My grandparents are making out!

894
00:38:34,267 --> 00:38:36,033
- ( ringing ) 
- Yes?

895
00:38:36,033 --> 00:38:38,433
"So, how far did you get? 
That leopard thing come off?"

896
00:38:38,433 --> 00:38:40,200
Yes, I'll get on it right away.

897
00:38:40,200 --> 00:38:42,800
"Got to go see if 
my refrigerator's running."

898
00:38:45,300 --> 00:38:47,567
- "Did you just call me?" 
- What's up?

899
00:38:47,567 --> 00:38:49,900
It's a truckload of 
radioactivated U-238.

900
00:38:49,900 --> 00:38:51,167
( gasping )

901
00:38:51,167 --> 00:38:52,967
It's headed for 
our local atomic plant.

902
00:38:52,967 --> 00:38:54,733
U-238?

903
00:38:54,733 --> 00:38:57,467
It's highly potential 
ingredient for atomic energy.

904
00:38:57,467 --> 00:38:58,500
"Or hot chocolate."

905
00:38:58,500 --> 00:39:00,800
It can be used in commercial 
and military use.

906
00:39:00,800 --> 00:39:03,067
 It'll revolutionize our power plant.

907
00:39:03,067 --> 00:39:05,067
We have orders to keep it 
under closest surveillance.

908
00:39:05,067 --> 00:39:07,633
 - "It's not better than radar, is it?" 
 - See if you can contact it.

909
00:39:07,633 --> 00:39:08,667
Yes, sir.

910
00:39:08,667 --> 00:39:11,367
He looks like a werewolf 
in mid-transition.

911
00:39:11,367 --> 00:39:13,667
Steven Tyler?

912
00:39:13,667 --> 00:39:14,967
"Like Moses at the rock,

913
00:39:14,967 --> 00:39:17,467
I had my first doubts 
about radar that day."

914
00:39:21,233 --> 00:39:24,900
"Oh, you've got the Radar 
Secret Service screen saver."

915
00:39:28,067 --> 00:39:30,700
"You kids turn off the radar. 
It's a school night."

916
00:39:30,700 --> 00:39:32,600
There it is.

917
00:39:32,600 --> 00:39:33,933
 Well, radar doesn't make the world

918
00:39:33,933 --> 00:39:35,500
any more interesting, does it?

919
00:39:35,500 --> 00:39:38,967
 - Why, it doesn't have an escort. 
 - It's a closely guarded secret.

920
00:39:38,967 --> 00:39:40,000
I think they're very wise

921
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:41,533
not calling attention 
to the shipment.

922
00:39:41,533 --> 00:39:44,433
 - I still think it's too risky. 
 - "You don't deserve radar."

923
00:39:44,433 --> 00:39:46,567
What's his bearing?

924
00:39:46,567 --> 00:39:49,067
 Jeez, the government 
 would collapse without this guy.

925
00:39:49,067 --> 00:39:50,733
Highway 13, heading east.

926
00:39:50,733 --> 00:39:52,433
Tell him to proceed 
at once to the depot.

927
00:39:52,433 --> 00:39:53,467
Yes, sir.

928
00:39:53,467 --> 00:39:54,933
 Look, supposing Static and I go out

929
00:39:54,933 --> 00:39:56,400
and keep an eye on him 
just in case.

930
00:39:56,400 --> 00:39:57,967
Okay. Call me when 
you get to the depot.

931
00:39:57,967 --> 00:39:59,300
 "And don't forget to use radar."

932
00:39:59,300 --> 00:40:01,633
Notify the truck that a radar 
car will meet them en route.

933
00:40:01,633 --> 00:40:03,100
Yes, sir.

934
00:40:03,100 --> 00:40:05,967
This guy is one of the best 
interns they've ever had.

935
00:40:05,967 --> 00:40:08,433
Calling OX-2.

936
00:40:08,433 --> 00:40:10,200
Boy, just imagine this 
on Omnimax.

937
00:40:10,200 --> 00:40:12,700
- Wow. 
- Ooh.

938
00:40:12,700 --> 00:40:14,700
We'll watch for them 
along the road.

939
00:40:14,700 --> 00:40:16,567
I'll flash you as soon 
as he picks us up.

940
00:40:16,567 --> 00:40:17,900
Right.

941
00:40:17,900 --> 00:40:21,400
I like that OX-2 guy. 
He's real nice.

942
00:40:21,400 --> 00:40:23,333
"What are you doing? 
What's that thing?

943
00:40:23,333 --> 00:40:25,600
What's that dial for?"

944
00:40:29,800 --> 00:40:34,500
Boy, vintage cars were really 
popular back then, huh?

945
00:40:34,500 --> 00:40:36,700
There's the tunnel.

946
00:40:36,700 --> 00:40:38,900
 It should take them about 20 minutes 
 to reach the "dey-po."

947
00:40:38,900 --> 00:40:40,933
Uh, "dee-po," sir.

948
00:40:40,933 --> 00:40:42,367
"Here's the tunnel.

949
00:40:42,367 --> 00:40:44,833
 Should take us about 20 minutes 
 to reach the dey-po."

950
00:40:44,833 --> 00:40:47,100
Keep in touch with them 
till they get there.

951
00:40:47,100 --> 00:40:49,433
 Oh, you'd like that, wouldn't you?

952
00:40:49,433 --> 00:40:51,633
OX-3. Calling OX-3.

953
00:40:51,633 --> 00:40:53,433
Come in, OX-3.

954
00:40:53,433 --> 00:40:55,800
Calling OX-3.

955
00:40:55,800 --> 00:40:57,667
"That's probably for me. 
It's my car."

956
00:40:57,667 --> 00:41:00,500
- This is OX-3. Go ahead. 
- "Hi, Huggy Bear."

957
00:41:01,967 --> 00:41:03,000
Yes. sir.

958
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:06,267
"Uh-huh. No. No way. 
She showed up with him?

959
00:41:06,267 --> 00:41:08,467
- Wow!" 
- Cut over to Highway 13.

960
00:41:10,067 --> 00:41:13,233
( gasps ) 
It's the Naegele capers!

961
00:41:15,333 --> 00:41:16,767
 It's certainly taking that truck

962
00:41:16,767 --> 00:41:18,300
a long time 
to get through that tunnel.

963
00:41:18,300 --> 00:41:20,000
Make it go faster.

964
00:41:22,100 --> 00:41:24,633
- Ah, wow. 
- Here it comes now.

965
00:41:24,633 --> 00:41:27,733
 "I can see that. I'm looking at it. 
 I invented radar."

966
00:41:29,600 --> 00:41:32,333
 ( goofy laugh ) 
 "Tell me about the rabbits again.

967
00:41:32,333 --> 00:41:34,400
Oh, it can wait."

968
00:41:37,733 --> 00:41:40,567
( humming along to soundtrack )

969
00:41:40,567 --> 00:41:42,233
Why is he turning off 
that highway?

970
00:41:42,233 --> 00:41:44,300
"Radar can't look 
into their hearts, sir."

971
00:41:44,300 --> 00:41:46,133
He's disobeying orders. 
Try to get through to him.

972
00:41:46,133 --> 00:41:47,167
Tell him to get back 
on the highway.

973
00:41:47,167 --> 00:41:48,200
Yes, sir.

974
00:41:48,200 --> 00:41:51,233
- ( goofy vocalization ) 
- OX-2, come in.

975
00:41:51,233 --> 00:41:53,633
- Calling OX-2. Come in. 
- "You go ahead."

976
00:41:53,633 --> 00:41:55,733
It's no use. His set 
must be fouled up.

977
00:41:55,733 --> 00:41:57,200
"I'm gonna go on break."

978
00:42:01,933 --> 00:42:05,533
 Well, we're losing him now. 
 He's... He's getting out of our beam.

979
00:42:05,533 --> 00:42:07,767
 Send out an alert. 
 Notify Bill of his change of direction.

