"Oh, I'll carry you."

1024
00:44:10,700 --> 00:44:15,300
♪ Oh, those Golden Grahams, 
oh, those Golden Grahams ♪

1025
00:44:15,300 --> 00:44:17,833
Only radar knows 
what the hell is going on.

1026
00:44:20,600 --> 00:44:23,000
That vehicle is so close 
to being an unmarked car.

1027
00:44:23,000 --> 00:44:25,500
"I only do these capers 
for the scenery."

1028
00:44:27,133 --> 00:44:30,333
 "My life is one big to-do list."

1029
00:44:33,467 --> 00:44:37,433
 - "The melon squad is in hot pursuit." 
 - Let's go, Blackie!

1030
00:44:37,433 --> 00:44:40,167
It's not "Blackie," 
It's "African-Americanie."

1031
00:44:43,467 --> 00:44:46,000
"Whoa! Whoa! Okay, I'll walk!"

1032
00:44:46,000 --> 00:44:48,833
 "And the goiter-mobile is there."

1033
00:44:49,967 --> 00:44:52,533
 "Hi. Listen, I've got some news.

1034
00:44:52,533 --> 00:44:55,933
"I came to tell you that 
we were maybe gonna-- Hey!"

1035
00:44:59,133 --> 00:45:01,033
Take care of the boys.

1036
00:45:02,267 --> 00:45:04,667
"Ah, we're done."

1037
00:45:04,667 --> 00:45:07,733
"How Green Was My Radar?"

1038
00:45:07,733 --> 00:45:09,633
"Oh, the Johnsons are early."

1039
00:45:14,700 --> 00:45:18,667
 "Oh, my atrizine representative." 
 ( goofy gibbering )

1040
00:45:19,667 --> 00:45:21,167
You know, maybe a parking ramp

1041
00:45:21,167 --> 00:45:23,600
 way out there wasn't a good idea.

1042
00:45:25,533 --> 00:45:28,500
♪♪

1043
00:45:31,500 --> 00:45:32,900
What's the matter 
with "Mr. Roboto"?

1044
00:45:32,900 --> 00:45:35,500
Nothing's the matter with it.

1045
00:45:35,500 --> 00:45:38,600
- Hey! Here he comes! 
- ♪ You don't love me ♪

1046
00:45:38,600 --> 00:45:40,700
Hey, what's going on? 
What is all this?

1047
00:45:40,700 --> 00:45:43,033
- ( exclaiming ) 
- Well, Mike, we know

1048
00:45:43,033 --> 00:45:45,933
 the hypno helio static stasis 
 might be getting to you, so we--

1049
00:45:45,933 --> 00:45:48,667
 And we know that you had to miss 
 your 10-year high school reunion,

1050
00:45:48,667 --> 00:45:51,133
 so we decided to have one for you.

1051
00:45:51,133 --> 00:45:53,333
Yeah. We found your yearbook, 
so we're all set

1052
00:45:53,333 --> 00:45:55,600
to simulate the actual 
reunion experience.

1053
00:45:55,600 --> 00:45:57,633
Wow, that's-that's great. 
Thanks.

1054
00:45:57,633 --> 00:45:59,900
- I'm really excited. 
- That's great.

1055
00:45:59,900 --> 00:46:02,400
Put your nametag on, 
there, Mike, and welcome to

1056
00:46:02,400 --> 00:46:05,067
the Baribou High School 
class of '83 reunion

1057
00:46:05,067 --> 00:46:07,900
 here at the Budget Hotel 
 Regency Room off County Trunk D!

1058
00:46:07,900 --> 00:46:10,933
- ( exclaims ) 
- Oh! Oh!

1059
00:46:10,933 --> 00:46:14,400
Oh! Oh, Jeez! Oh! 
Nelson? Mike Nelson?

1060
00:46:14,400 --> 00:46:17,700
Buddy! Nelson, man! 
What's going on, man?

1061
00:46:17,700 --> 00:46:20,033
Man, I envy you, Nelson.

1062
00:46:20,033 --> 00:46:21,667
 You made it. 
 You're got out of this town, man.

1063
00:46:21,667 --> 00:46:24,033
Wow! I married Pam,

1064
00:46:24,033 --> 00:46:26,100
 just like everybody said I would.

1065
00:46:26,100 --> 00:46:28,733
It's okay, I guess. 
Hey, I never see you down

1066
00:46:28,733 --> 00:46:30,367
at the Rendezvous anymore, man.

1067
00:46:30,367 --> 00:46:32,633
That's 'cause I don't live 
around here anymore.

1068
00:46:32,633 --> 00:46:34,667
Yeah, that's probably it.

1069
00:46:34,667 --> 00:46:36,733
Man, I envy you, Nelson. 
You made it.

1070
00:46:36,733 --> 00:46:38,500
You got out of this town, man.

1071
00:46:38,500 --> 00:46:40,467
- Mike? 
- Oh, boy.

1072
00:46:40,467 --> 00:46:43,967
Mike Nelson! Remember me?

1073
00:46:43,967 --> 00:46:45,933
Janine. Janine LaFond.

1074
00:46:45,933 --> 00:46:47,733
Right, how you doing, 
Janine LaFond?

1075
00:46:47,733 --> 00:46:49,733
Oh, yeah, except for now, 
it's Janine LaFond-Spike.

1076
00:46:49,733 --> 00:46:51,467
How are you?

1077
00:46:51,467 --> 00:46:53,367
I'm good. 
It's good to see you again.

1078
00:46:53,367 --> 00:46:56,367
Hey, how come you never 
asked me out, huh?

1079
00:46:56,367 --> 00:46:59,167
I just always thought 
you were totally stuck-up.

1080
00:46:59,167 --> 00:47:01,467
 Oh, hey, I'd better go call the sitter.

1081
00:47:01,467 --> 00:47:04,633
 She's got her hands full with those 
 nine rugrats and everything.

1082
00:47:04,633 --> 00:47:06,533
- See ya! 
- Yeah, right.

1083
00:47:06,533 --> 00:47:08,500
Nine kids in 10 year--

1084
00:47:08,500 --> 00:47:09,800
Hi, Mike.

1085
00:47:09,800 --> 00:47:11,900
Hi, um, uh, uh, uh...

1086
00:47:11,900 --> 00:47:14,467
- Guess. 
- Um...

1087
00:47:14,467 --> 00:47:15,600
Rick. How you doing, Rick?

1088
00:47:15,600 --> 00:47:17,200
- Good to see you. 
- No.

1089
00:47:17,200 --> 00:47:20,100
I sat three seats behind you

1090
00:47:20,100 --> 00:47:22,733
and four back 
in Health and Family Living.

1091
00:47:22,733 --> 00:47:25,033
It's John. How are you, John?

1092
00:47:25,033 --> 00:47:27,500
- No. 
- Hey, everybody. Brenda again.

1093
00:47:27,500 --> 00:47:30,867
Okay, here is the answer 
to the trivia question.

1094
00:47:30,867 --> 00:47:34,700
Cindy Gannett called her car 
"Land Yacht."

1095
00:47:34,700 --> 00:47:37,467
Okay. Now we're gonna 
get going with the music.

1096
00:47:37,467 --> 00:47:39,400
Here's Impaler!

1097
00:47:39,400 --> 00:47:41,233
( exclaiming )

1098
00:47:41,233 --> 00:47:43,400
It's Jim. 
No, I can't, 'cause...

1099
00:47:43,400 --> 00:47:46,467
I've got to get some punch, 
and it's movie sign!

1100
00:47:58,333 --> 00:48:01,333
( chuckling ) 
Oh, fun, huh?

1101
00:48:01,333 --> 00:48:03,233
 "Well, as long as we're all here, 
 let's draw names for Christmas."

1102
00:48:03,233 --> 00:48:04,300
Where's Blackie?

1103
00:48:04,300 --> 00:48:06,333
Squad car showed up, and I 
had to get away in a hurry.

1104
00:48:06,333 --> 00:48:07,367
He couldn't make it.

1105
00:48:07,367 --> 00:48:08,500
Do you think 
they picked him up?

1106
00:48:08,500 --> 00:48:09,833
Must have.

1107
00:48:09,833 --> 00:48:12,000
That's a bad break for him, 
but a good break for us.

1108
00:48:12,000 --> 00:48:13,533
How do you figure that?

1109
00:48:13,533 --> 00:48:15,033
Won't have to cut 
the melon so thin.

1110
00:48:15,033 --> 00:48:16,200
They've got melons.

1111
00:48:16,200 --> 00:48:18,200
Yeah, but suppose they start 
sweating him and he sings?

1112
00:48:18,200 --> 00:48:20,700
Don't worry about him singing. 
He's crazy about Marge,

1113
00:48:20,700 --> 00:48:22,767
and he wouldn't want 
anything to happen to her.

1114
00:48:22,767 --> 00:48:23,800
Hey, Sid Melton.

1115
00:48:23,800 --> 00:48:25,067
I'll meet you later 
at the apartment.

1116
00:48:25,067 --> 00:48:26,700
Okay.

1117
00:48:26,700 --> 00:48:29,000
"What page do 
our lines begin on?"

1118
00:48:29,000 --> 00:48:30,133
They grabbed off one of my men,

1119
00:48:30,133 --> 00:48:32,333
but we got the truck 
hidden in a barn.

1120
00:48:32,333 --> 00:48:34,367
When do you want to pick it up?

1121
00:48:34,367 --> 00:48:36,400
You make it sound so easy.

1122
00:48:36,400 --> 00:48:38,600
- Well, what's wrong with it? 
- The radar patrol.

1123
00:48:38,600 --> 00:48:40,300
Where do you think 
those cops came from?

1124
00:48:40,300 --> 00:48:41,767
You're gonna have it 
halfway across the ocean

1125
00:48:41,767 --> 00:48:43,633
before they get wise.

1126
00:48:43,633 --> 00:48:44,667
Michael is right.

1127
00:48:44,667 --> 00:48:46,433
They'd grab you the minute 
you made a move.

1128
00:48:46,433 --> 00:48:48,000
They've got 
the whole town covered.

1129
00:48:48,000 --> 00:48:49,833
Peggy Lee runs the mob.

1130
00:48:49,833 --> 00:48:51,767
Looks like I'm outnumbered 
around here.

1131
00:48:51,767 --> 00:48:53,167
Well, what do you think 
we ought to do?

1132
00:48:53,167 --> 00:48:54,200
Change pants?

1133
00:48:54,200 --> 00:48:56,700
My first suggestion is to 
get rid of that radar truck.

1134
00:48:56,700 --> 00:48:57,867
- Blasphemer! 
- He must die.

1135
00:48:57,867 --> 00:49:00,067
And then what?

1136
00:49:00,067 --> 00:49:02,733
I have a yacht about 
six miles up the river.

1137
00:49:02,733 --> 00:49:04,767
- It's called Monkey Business. 
- That's interesting.

1138
00:49:04,767 --> 00:49:06,600
 You can reach it from an old pier

1139
00:49:06,600 --> 00:49:09,033
about 20 miles out of town 
on the river road.

1140
00:49:09,033 --> 00:49:11,033
We'll need some help 
to get it aboard ship.

1141
00:49:11,033 --> 00:49:14,400
 Just get it near that pier. 
 My boys will take care of the rest.

1142
00:49:14,400 --> 00:49:16,167
And then I get paid, huh?

1143
00:49:16,167 --> 00:49:17,733
What's the matter? 
Don't you trust me?

1144
00:49:17,733 --> 00:49:20,467
This is one of those important 
moments in any relationship.

1145
00:49:20,467 --> 00:49:22,967
I'd better not answer that.

1146
00:49:22,967 --> 00:49:24,733
Look, we got it halfway to you.

1147
00:49:24,733 --> 00:49:26,867
I want half the dough now.

1148
00:49:26,867 --> 00:49:30,133
"Well, here. 
Dan Fogelberg tickets."

1149
00:49:30,133 --> 00:49:33,033
"Got to move my condoms. 
Surprised I have any left."

1150
00:49:35,233 --> 00:49:37,200
 We're stepping out tonight, sugar.

1151
00:49:37,200 --> 00:49:39,700
I'm sorry. 
I promised Michael I'd...

1152
00:49:39,700 --> 00:49:41,533
 I'll pick you up about 8:00, my dear.

1153
00:49:41,533 --> 00:49:43,800
"It's not the radar, 
it's the size of the amplitude,

1154
00:49:43,800 --> 00:49:45,167
if you know what I mean."

1155
00:49:47,433 --> 00:49:50,667
"That's okay. I don't care."

1156
00:49:50,667 --> 00:49:53,900
"And never darken 
my carpets again!"

1157
00:49:53,900 --> 00:49:56,833
 Remember me? 
 I'm your boyfriend, Mickey Moran.

1158
00:49:56,833 --> 00:49:59,000
"Oh, that's right. 
I'm terrible with names."

1159
00:49:59,000 --> 00:50:01,767
I don't like the way 
this deal is turning out.

1160
00:50:01,767 --> 00:50:04,700
 - You like his money, don't you? 
 - Well, sure.

1161
00:50:04,700 --> 00:50:08,333
- What do you like about him? 
- He's the contact we need.

1162
00:50:08,333 --> 00:50:10,200
I'm just as anxious as you 
to get this job over with

1163
00:50:10,200 --> 00:50:11,233
so we can all be paid off.

1164
00:50:11,233 --> 00:50:12,467
Uh, he's on fire.

1165
00:50:12,467 --> 00:50:14,733
Your jealousy is 
going to ruin everything.

1166
00:50:14,733 --> 00:50:17,267
Now, look, baby, 
when this job is over,

1167
00:50:17,267 --> 00:50:19,967
 you figure on combing lover boy 
 out of your hair

1168
00:50:19,967 --> 00:50:21,333
with a fine-toothed comb.

1169
00:50:21,333 --> 00:50:24,633
 "I haven't combed my hair in 13 years. 
 You know that."

1170
00:50:26,800 --> 00:50:29,833
 Her hair is soft-serve. 
 They should put that curl on it.

1171
00:50:31,333 --> 00:50:33,900
"I'm not drinking. Nope."

1172
00:50:33,900 --> 00:50:35,633
- You get anything out of him? 
- ( both exclaim )

1173
00:50:35,633 --> 00:50:37,000
No, not a peep.

1174
00:50:37,000 --> 00:50:39,033
 I'm having them check the files 
 for a possible lead.

1175
00:50:39,033 --> 00:50:41,733
- He may have a record. 
- ( whistles )

1176
00:50:41,733 --> 00:50:43,967
"No waffles!"

1177
00:50:43,967 --> 00:50:46,667
- Anybody we know? 
- What? Who?

1178
00:50:46,667 --> 00:50:48,833
No, no. It's just a picture

1179
00:50:48,833 --> 00:50:50,767
that I got out 
of his little black book.

1180
00:50:50,767 --> 00:50:52,833
- Whose little black book? 
- "Bob Packwood's."

1181
00:50:52,833 --> 00:50:55,100
The guy we picked up. 
The fellow on the road.

1182
00:50:55,100 --> 00:50:57,133
Where did you get it?

1183
00:50:57,133 --> 00:51:00,467
 I think he dropped it. 
 I picked it up off of the floor.

1184
00:51:00,467 --> 00:51:02,367
You picked it up off the floor?

1185
00:51:02,367 --> 00:51:04,100
"That's my wife, you bastard."

1186
00:51:04,100 --> 00:51:05,600
This may be the answer 
to our problem.

1187
00:51:05,600 --> 00:51:06,667
What is it?

1188
00:51:06,667 --> 00:51:08,667
 - "A coupon for yams." 
 - Probably one of his girlfriends.

1189
00:51:08,667 --> 00:51:12,467
"Can I help you? 
Smoking or non?"

1190
00:51:12,467 --> 00:51:14,500
We might be able to learn 
a lot from her.

1191
00:51:14,500 --> 00:51:16,067
- "Busing tables..." 
- Who couldn't?

1192
00:51:16,067 --> 00:51:17,300
Check every restaurant in town.

1193
00:51:17,300 --> 00:51:18,900
It shouldn't be tough 
running her down.

1194
00:51:18,900 --> 00:51:20,167
"Pretty run down already."

1195
00:51:20,167 --> 00:51:22,367
( chuckles ) 
But I kid.

1196
00:51:24,167 --> 00:51:25,900
- ♪ Where are you going? ♪ 
- ♪ I don't know ♪

1197
00:51:25,900 --> 00:51:27,900
- ♪ How you gonna get there? ♪ 
- ♪ I ain't certain ♪

1198
00:51:27,900 --> 00:51:30,733
 ♪ All I know is that I'm on my way ♪

1199
00:51:32,600 --> 00:51:35,200
"No, sir. 
I never seen her."

1200
00:51:35,200 --> 00:51:37,433
Well, why don't they try 
using that radar

1201
00:51:37,433 --> 00:51:39,133
they're always bragging about?

1202
00:51:41,867 --> 00:51:45,067
"Get out of here, 
you filthy little man."

1203
00:51:45,067 --> 00:51:47,933
"I thought they served fun 
at Shakey's."

1204
00:51:51,300 --> 00:51:54,167
"That's the oddest thing 
anyone's ever showed me."

1205
00:51:57,133 --> 00:51:59,567
Boy, she can really 
hold a smile for a long time.

1206
00:51:59,567 --> 00:52:01,867
- It's a picture. 
- Oh.

1207
00:52:03,767 --> 00:52:05,933
"The layout of this place..."

1208
00:52:05,933 --> 00:52:07,667
"Nice salad bar."

1209
00:52:09,733 --> 00:52:13,400
"Look, would you just 
bring me my meat loaf?"

1210
00:52:13,400 --> 00:52:15,400
"Meat?"

1211
00:52:15,400 --> 00:52:17,067
"I've got a coupon here."

1212
00:52:17,067 --> 00:52:19,333
"All right. Two for one."

1213
00:52:19,333 --> 00:52:22,700
"Get over there. 
Stake out the dessert tray."

1214
00:52:22,700 --> 00:52:25,967
♪ Are you happy in your work ♪

1215
00:52:25,967 --> 00:52:27,900
( humming )

1216
00:52:29,433 --> 00:52:31,300
"Butter. Mm."

1217
00:52:31,300 --> 00:52:33,267
Those two haven't talked 
in years, have they?

